Understanding the Output

Once you open ECG_Analysis_Results.xlsx, navigate to the First_Derivatives sheet:

The Data: You will see the time-series slope values.

The Chart: An embedded Excel chart will show a sharp peak where the R-wave occurs.

Physiological Significance: The peak in the derivative chart corresponds to the most 
rapid change in heart voltage (the QRS complex). By visualizing this in Excel, you can 
verify that the mathematical derivative is correctly "triggering" on the heartbeat.
